format session-log-v1
stamp 20260821.203103
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The exclusion survey, and three merges declined on measurement
prompt kg
think Took the lap I had named: survey the other scan scripts for exclusion lists that are the same claim wearing a second copy. Ten carried exclusion clauses; three carried real ones.
think Went in expecting to unify and came out declining, which is what a survey is for. The instinct after a successful merge is to merge more, and that instinct is exactly what wants checking rather than following.
think Measured before judging shipped_binary_claim_scan. It shares .git seed vendor and adds gratitude, and the question is whether gratitude belongs in the dated-path census too. It contributes 113 dated references of which SIX are genuinely broken -- so folding it in would drop real breakage out of the count. A merge that hides breakage is not a merge.
think Saw the vols pair disagree with each other and thought I had found a weakness in a two-tools-one-answer claim, then checked what each is actually passed. crosscount walks a fixture tree while truth walks the real one, so a narrower list fits a smaller corpus. Both witnesses stand green. Different corpora, not a mismatch.
think Named the test that decides these, since without one the next round re-litigates: two lists merge when they answer the same QUESTION, not when they share entries. The dated-path pair did -- both ask what is not the field and what is the instrument -- and their volatile half, the fixture names, grows with every tool that plants one. The stable three-directory base costs nothing to repeat.
obs Recorded the survey result inside the shared exclusions file rather than only in this log, because that file is where a future merge would begin and a reason left only in a session log is a reason nobody reads at the moment of deciding.
obs Preventing a wrong merge is worth as much as making a right one, and it is quieter -- no commit shows the damage that did not happen.
loom survey=exclusion_lists scripts_with_clauses=10 real_lists=3 merged=0 declined=3
loom measured=gratitude dated_refs=113 broken=6 verdict=would_hide_breakage
loom vols=two_tools truth_root=real_tree crosscount_root=fixture_tree both_green=yes
file tools/fixtures/dated_path_exclusions.sh the survey result, recorded where the next merge would start
recommend check-in (checkpoint) the survey is done and declined three merges with reasons, so the shared list stays two consumers wide and the other three keep their own scopes. Nothing is pending and every guard stands green; the next constructive door is a fresh one rather than more tidying of this pair.
